          "dueAt": "2026-11-04T16:00:00.000Z",
          "sentAt": "2026-11-04T16:02:29.675Z",
          "request": {
            "channelId": "6aaa90f5ea19ca0bde582f0e",
            "schedulingType": "automatic",
            "mode": "customScheduled",
            "dueAt": "2026-11-04T16:00:00Z",
            "text": "A torn cloak still has miles left.\n\nSwipe to see what a patch can save. In this imagined moment in Roo, the old wool is sound; one torn shoulder doesn't have to end its travels.\n\nWhat have you kept by repairing it? A few words will do.\n\nConcept art from The Land of Roo.\n\n#TheLandOfRoo #NordicFantasy #FantasyArt #Worldbuilding",
            "assets": [
              {
                "image": {
                  "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/fanderflash/thelandofroo/693211b82d6459da9f9ad393dfdc559060dfe9ba/assets/social/2026-11-04/17-cloak-01.jpg",
                  "metadata": {
                    "altText": "A Rooan woman examines a torn green wool cloak beside an ochre patch and thread. Text: Would you throw it away? Swipe to see what she saved."
                  }
                }
              },
              {
                "image": {
                  "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/fanderflash/thelandofroo/693211b82d6459da9f9ad393dfdc559060dfe9ba/assets/social/2026-11-04/17-cloak-02.jpg",
                  "metadata": {
                    "altText": "The same woman smiles over the same cloak, now repaired with an ochre patch. Text: One patch. Another journey. What have you kept by repairing it?"
                  }
                }
              }
            ],
            "metadata": {
              "instagram": {
                "type": "post",
                "shouldShareToFeed": true,
                "isAiGenerated": true
